course: dictionary
lesson: 8161
title: Working out a word from its clues
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You can often work out a new word from the words around it. «In Israel most adults serve in the army, and many are called back as reservists in wartime.» The clues are called back and wartime, so a reservist must be someone who serves in the armed forces when the country needs them.
explain: Look at the parts of the word too. Reserve means to keep something back for later use, and the ending -ist often means a person who does or belongs to something, as in artist or cyclist. Together, they point to a person kept back ready for service.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into a sentence. «Many nurses and teachers are reservists, and they train some weekends.» A reservist has a normal job and trains part-time, so the sentence still makes sense. Your meaning fits, so you can trust it.
fact: A reservist has a normal job, such as teacher, builder or nurse.
fact: Reservists train as soldiers, sailors or airmen, often in their spare time, such as some weekends.
fact: A reservist can be «called up» to serve in the armed forces when they are needed.
fact: Reservists may be called up in wartime or after floods and other disasters.
fact: Useful phrases are «army reservist», «a reservist soldier» and «call up reservists».
exercise: A reservist usually has which kind of job in everyday life? | A job on a ship that never comes home | A full-time job in the army only | *A normal job, such as teacher or builder | No job at all
exercise: «Reservists can be called up in wartime.» What does called up mean? | *Asked to come back and serve | Asked to sing a song | Forgotten and left behind | Given a holiday
exercise: Find and copy the word that tells you when reservists may be called back. | army | *wartime | adults | Israel
test: «Reservists train some weekends, so they are ready to help when needed.» What do reservists do at weekends? | Go shopping only | Play football for the school | *Train as soldiers, sailors or airmen | Sleep in and rest all day
test: Which phrase means a soldier who is part of the reserve force? | the ancient army | a school soldier with a bag | *a reservist soldier, trained and ready to be called up | a reservist soldier
exam: Which sentence best explains what a reservist is? | A full-time soldier who never leaves the barracks and never has a job | A child who lives on a farm and feeds the animals | *A person with a normal job who has trained for the armed forces and can be called up when needed | A nurse who only works in a hospital and never trains
